{"case_id":"sca-auth-001","review_status":"REVIEWED","verdict":"SCORING_FALSE_NEGATIVE","reviewer":"Tony","reviewed_at":"2026-08-24T18:28:31.4661951Z","correctness":"CORRECT","scope":"APPROPRIATE","evidence_support":"SUPPORTED","version_handling":"CORRECT","citation_quality":"GOOD","notes":"Human product review confirmed that API tokens are used for API access, while username and password are used to log in through the UI. The production answer correctly described API-token authentication; the machine failure was caused by literal expected wording."}
{"case_id":"sca-auth-002","review_status":"REVIEWED","verdict":"TRUE_PASS","reviewer":"Tony","reviewed_at":"2026-08-24T18:29:55.6362516Z","correctness":"CORRECT","scope":"APPROPRIATE","evidence_support":"SUPPORTED","version_handling":"CORRECT","citation_quality":"GOOD","notes":"Human product review confirmed the answer is correct. It identifies POST /api/tokens/authenticate and the API-token Authorization header without adding unnecessary scope."}
