{"case_id":"sca-auth-005","review_status":"REVIEWED","verdict":"SCORING_FALSE_NEGATIVE","reviewer":"Tony","reviewed_at":"2026-08-24T18:33:28.4569253Z","correctness":"CORRECT","scope":"APPROPRIATE","evidence_support":"SUPPORTED","version_handling":"CORRECT","citation_quality":"GOOD","notes":"Human product review confirmed that user access tokens do not expire, but a user can delete or regenerate them, and tokens associated with an account should no longer be valid if the owning user loses access. The production answer conveyed these conditions; the machine failure was caused by literal wording."}
{"case_id":"sca-auth-006","review_status":"REVIEWED","verdict":"SCORING_FALSE_NEGATIVE","reviewer":"Tony","reviewed_at":"2026-08-24T18:36:09.2121006Z","correctness":"CORRECT","scope":"APPROPRIATE","evidence_support":"SUPPORTED","version_handling":"CORRECT","citation_quality":"GOOD","notes":"Human product review confirmed that tokens associated with an inactivated user should no longer work. The production answer correctly stated that the tokens are invalidated; the exact-string scorer failed on wording. Human also proposed a future runtime test using a newly created test user and token, followed by inactivation from the original administrator account and a rejected authentication attempt. That runtime test is captured separately and was not executed."}
